From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winspool, winprint, wineumpd, splwow64: printer and document events; makers' 64-bit drivers for 32-bit programs

What makers' drivers expect of the spooler and of GDI, and what a 32-bit
program needs to use a 64-bit maker's driver:

- winspool: a new printer's driver is told so (DrvPrinterEvent,
  PRINTER_EVENT_INITIALIZE) once the printer is there with its settings,
  and a deleted one's (PRINTER_EVENT_DELETE). Makers' drivers make their
  registry entries and files there (Epson's writes its status URLs, Brother's
  label driver its timeouts).
- winspool: DocumentEvent (a stub) calls the configuration DLL's
  DrvDocumentEvent; GDI calls it for each printing call (1035). The
  document-event constants and structures are in winddiui.h.
- winspool: a 32-bit program cannot load a 64-bit driver's configuration
  DLL, nor the makers' plug-ins it loads. DocumentProperties (settings and
  Printing preferences), DeviceCapabilities and PrinterProperties are
  answered by our 64-bit print host (splwow64), which loads it; the
  settings and the answer go over in files. Brother's own preferences
  sheet opens from a 32-bit program, and its papers and settings reach it.
- winprint, wineumpd, splwow64: a DEVMODE with the public settings alone
  (a program's own, or one spooled by a program that could not reach the
  driver) is merged into the driver's own settings (DocumentProperties)
  before the driver is enabled. Brother's label printers' driver crashed
  without them.
- winprint: when our 64-bit host prints a 32-bit program's job, it holds a
  job of its own for it on the printer, so a driver that looks its job up
  (GetJob, Brother's) finds it; the driver's DrvStartDoc failed.

Test: test/drvpkg-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_PRINTEREVENT, HOSTCONFIG,
HOSTJOB, MERGEDEVMODE, CAPSDEVMODE in wineumpd and in splwow64).
